mmcv-full 1.7.2 on PyTorch >= 2.6: torch's internal _get_stream() takes a torch.device, while
mmcv's Scatter passes an int GPU index, so MMDataParallel scatter fails. BEVServe's own inference
path does not use MMDataParallel; the patch is applied so the image matches the validated stack.
Apply with `git apply` in the mmcv v1.7.2 source tree (commit 4c01b026) before building.

--- a/mmcv/parallel/_functions.py
+++ b/mmcv/parallel/_functions.py
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
         streams = None
         if input_device == -1 and target_gpus != [-1]:
             # Perform CPU to GPU copies in a background stream
-            streams = [_get_stream(device) for device in target_gpus]
+            streams = [_get_stream(torch.device("cuda", device) if isinstance(device, int) else device) for device in target_gpus]
 
         outputs = scatter(input, target_gpus, streams)
         # Synchronize with the copy stream
